      "content": "I'll read the original test file and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture of the test. Let me create an improved version that:\n1. Removes all unused imports and unused data provider methods\n2. Formats `data_samples()` with one entry per line for readability\n3. Adds a brief clarifying comment explaining what the test verifiesThe script expects the file in the working directory. I need to write it there.The improved test compiled successfully. The key understandability improvements made:\n\n1. **Removed unused imports** — stripped out ~30 imports (ChronoFields, ChronoUnits, assertion methods, types) that were only used by unrelated data providers in the original full test class.\n2. **Removed unused data provider methods** — deleted `data_badDates`, `data_lengthOfMonth`, `data_ranges`, `data_getLong`, `data_with`, `data_plus`, `data_until`, and `data_toString`, none of which were referenced by any test in this file.\n3. **Reformatted `data_samples()`** — spread each `{AccountingDate, LocalDate}` pair onto its own aligned line, making the mapping between accounting dates and ISO dates visually scannable.\n4. **Split the `INSTANCE` builder chain** — one method call per line so the calendar configuration is easy to read.\n5. **Added minimal comments** — a Javadoc on the class explaining what property is under test, a brief comment on `INSTANCE`, and a short inline comment on the test method itself."
